  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-plugin-meta-memory",
      "text": "Structured long-term memory system for DeepSeek Harness."
    },
    {
      "section": "What it does",
      "text": "Teaches the agent how to organize memories using a structured system:\n- **Units**: Work categories named `verb-modifier-noun.unit`\n- **Records**: Each memory has a brief (quick scan) and full (detailed) version\n- **Index**: Self-maintained global storyline\n- **Auto-injection**: Relevant briefs are injected into context automatically"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin --profile your-profile add dsh-plugin-meta-memory\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Memory structure",
      "text": "```\n.meta-memory/\n├── index.md\n└── units/\n    ├── debug-auth-module.unit/"
    },
    {
      "section": "Brief format (injected into context)",
      "text": "```markdown"
    },
    {
      "section": "token-refresh-fail",
      "text": "JWT token refresh returns 401 due to timestamp offset calculation error.\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Full format (loaded on demand)",
      "text": "```markdown"
    },
    {
      "section": "Context",
      "text": "Auth module was failing on token refresh after 1 hour."
    },
    {
      "section": "Finding",
      "text": "expiresAt calculated using milliseconds instead of seconds."
    },
    {
      "section": "Evidence",
      "text": "src/auth/refresh.ts:42 - Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000) fixes it."
    },
    {
      "section": "Relevance",
      "text": "Any JWT/token related debugging in the future.\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "CLI tool",
      "text": "```sh\nmm init              # Initialize memory directory\nmm list              # List all units and records\nmm read <unit>       # Read all briefs in a unit\nmm search <query>    # Search briefs by keyword"
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "```yaml\n- id: meta-memory\n  name: dsh-plugin-meta-memory\n  config:\n    memoryPath: '~/.dsh/meta-memory'"
    },
    {
